course: dictionary
lesson: 12762
title: Earlier and time words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word earlier tells you that something happened before now, or before another time. «We finished our project earlier today.» Earlier today means some time before this moment, so the project is already done.
explain: Earlier can also mean sooner than usual. «She woke up earlier than her brother.» Look for words like than, today or on to see what earlier is being compared with.
explain: Earlier can come before a noun, like an adjective. «Read the earlier chapter again before the test.» The earlier chapter is the one that came before the chapter you are on now.
fact: Earlier is the comparison form of early: early, earlier, earliest.
fact: «Earlier» means at a time before now or before another time.
fact: «Earlier» can be an adverb, as in «He arrived earlier», or an adjective, as in «the earlier question».
fact: In a maths problem, «2 hours earlier» means you take away 2 hours from the time.
exercise: «We left earlier than the others, so we missed the rain.» What does earlier mean here? | *Before the others | Very slowly | After the others | At the same time as the others
exercise: A clock shows 5 o'clock. What time is «2 hours earlier»? | 7 o'clock | *3 o'clock | 5 past 2 | 2 o'clock
exercise: «Look back at the earlier question and check your answer.» Which question is the earlier one? | The one with the most words | The one that comes after | *The one that came before | The hardest one on the page
test: «Ravi finished his homework earlier on, so he could play outside.» What does earlier on mean? | Some time after now | *Some time before now | Never | Exactly at this moment
test: «She reached the station earlier than her friend.» Who got there first? | Nobody | The friend | *She | Both at the same time
exam: Which sentence uses earlier as an adjective, before a noun? | He is earlier than me. | *Check the earlier page first. | She got up earlier. | We finished earlier today.
